  "workload": "60 s of the default 64-channel synthetic layout (seed 2026): 384,000 frames, 51,072,000 samples, 13,856 feature windows; sent unpaced (as fast as ingest accepts) over TCP; every batch stored durably (Parquet + fsync) before it is acknowledged",
  "kind": "per-socket pipeline experiment, second run: adds per-socket-shared-store (not a milestone)",
  "date": "2026-11-22",
  "question": "Do a shared group-commit store and time-batched feature writes fix the per-socket pipeline's disk penalty?",
  "commits": {
    "paralanes": "33a8226 (branch exp-per-socket-pipeline)",
    "diagsteno": "f6d1014 (main)",
    "stagelanes": "b09f58f (main)",
    "bytelanes": "main with M7 FFT"
  },
  "commands": [
    "cd paralanes/experiments/per-socket-pipeline && cargo build --release",
    "for r in 1 2 3; do for store in /dev/shm/psp ~/.cache/psp-disk; do for l in baseline per-socket per-socket-unpinned per-socket-shared-store; do ./target/release/per-socket-pipeline --layout $l --store-dir $store --seconds 60; done; done; done"
  ],
  "layouts": {
    "baseline": "diagsteno::ingest::Ingest: reader thread, writer thread (store + ack), ONE feature thread; unpinned; one sender with all 64 channels",
    "per-socket": "2 shards, shard s = accel 16s..16s+15 and strain 32+16s..32+16s+15, all threads pinned to socket s: ingest core, store core, 4 feature cores, sender core; stagelanes-ring SPSC rings between stages; own TCP port and store directory per shard",
    "per-socket-unpinned": "the same 2 shards with no pinning",
    "per-socket-shared-store": "shards' ingest and 4 feature cores pinned to their own socket; ONE store thread on socket 0 core 1 writes both shards' 100 ms batches as one durable Parquet file (one fsync per batch) and acks each shard; ONE feature writer on socket 0 stores all feature rows once per second"
  },
  "noise_note": "Disk runs varied far more than in the first run an hour earlier (baseline 4.61-12.89 s now vs 4.74-5.07 s then), so differences between layouts on disk are not resolved by 3 repeats.",
